# Allowlist for leg (a) of the read-instruction check in
# scripts/always-loaded-budget.sh: tracked .md files that an always-loaded file
# may NAME without @-importing, because the mention is a pointer to on-demand
# material rather than a mandated read.
#
# One path per line, reason in a trailing comment. Leg (a) deliberately fires on
# pointers as well as mandates: over-firing costs one line here, under-firing
# ships an instruction surface that some agents obey and others do not, with
# nothing downstream able to tell those states apart.
#
# This is NOT a place to silence a real mandated read. If a file must be read,
# @-import it (and pay for it in the budget) or downgrade it to a pointer.
.claude/agents/oracle.md       # named as a touched-file entry in the e2e matrix table, not a read
.claude/agents/test-critic.md  # same
docs/todo/punchlist.md         # "see ... for in-flight punchlist" — an on-demand pointer
# QUM-1155: CLAUDE.md's opening names DESCRIPTION.md as where the project
# overview lives. It is a POINTER, not a mandated read: the line reads
# "Project overview: `DESCRIPTION.md`, on demand", and the cut deliberately
# did NOT @-import it — importing would add 195 lines to the very surface this
# budget exists to bound, which is 2.7x the whole post-cut CLAUDE.md.
DESCRIPTION.md                 # project overview — an on-demand pointer, deliberately not imported
